00:05:17,647 --> 00:05:23,647
It's a short trip from zero... to hero.

2
00:10:35,294 --> 00:10:41,294
Minutemen is a family, tv movie, comedy film directed by Lev L. Spiro.

3
00:15:52,941 --> 00:15:58,941
When three high-school friends invent a time-machine, they decide to use it to go back
in time and prevent other youngsters from making humiliating mistakes.

4
00:21:10,588 --> 00:21:16,588
Virgil Fox, played by Jason Dolley.

5
00:26:28,235 --> 00:26:34,235
Zeke Thompson, played by Nicholas Braun.

6
00:31:45,882 --> 00:31:51,882
Charlie Tuttle, played by Luke Benward.

7
00:37:03,529 --> 00:37:09,529
Stephanie Jameson, played by Chelsea Kane.

8
00:42:21,176 --> 00:42:27,176
Derek Beaugard, played by Steven R. McQueen.

9
00:47:38,823 --> 00:47:44,823
Vice Principal Tolkan, played by J. P. Manoux.

10
00:52:56,470 --> 00:53:02,470
Minutemen is a 2008 science-fiction Disney Channel Original Movie.

11
00:58:14,117 --> 00:58:20,117
The movie was the most viewed program on American cable TV for the
week ending January 27, 2008, with 6.48 million viewers.

12
01:03:31,764 --> 01:03:37,764
The film was written by John Killoran (writing the teleplay) and David Diamond
and David Weissman (writing the story) and directed by Lev L.

13
01:08:49,411 --> 01:08:55,411
Spiro, who received a Directors Guild nomination for
Outstanding Achievement in Children's Programs for it.

14
01:14:07,058 --> 01:14:13,058
Andrew Gunn, Ann Marie Sanderlin and Doug Sloan are the executive producers.

15
01:19:24,705 --> 01:19:30,705
The movie was originally slated for release in March 2008, but the film
premiered on Disney Channel in United States on January 25.

16
01:24:42,352 --> 01:24:48,352
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
